// D-SCHEDULE1 (ratified 2026-07-11, card #505) — schedule-as-code.
// `@Every(…)` is a directive marker on a `@Task fn` (D-JPK-TASKRUN1): one
// declaration feeds `jet dev` (runs due tasks in the dev loop), the service
// runtime (D-SERVICE1), and a jetos timer projection. `@Every(5min)` takes a
// duration literal (D-UNITLIT1: `ns`/`us`/`ms`/`s`/`min`); `@Every("03:00")`
// takes a daily wall-clock time. A `@Task fn` with no `@Every(…)` is a plain
// manually-invoked task (`jetpack run manual_only`).
//
// Calling a `@Task fn` directly — as `run()` does below — behaves exactly
// like calling an ordinary function; the schedule only changes when a
// runtime consumer invokes it *automatically*. `jet dev`'s due-task tick is
// exercised by tests/dev.rs, not by this golden AOT run (I5's ordinary-run
// convention for dev-loop-only behavior — see devloop/persist.jet).
@Task
@Every(5min)
fn prune_sessions() {
    print("pruning sessions")
}

@Task
@Every("03:00")
fn nightly_backup() {
    print("running nightly backup")
}

@Task
fn manual_only() {
    print("ran manually")
}

fn run() {
    prune_sessions()
    nightly_backup()
    manual_only()
}
// --- expected output --------------------------------------------------
// pruning sessions
// running nightly backup
// ran manually
